# Surface profile: USE needed on top of the common live image. The Surface itself never compiles
# anything (the installer copies the squashfs); small source builds happen once, on the ISO build host.
net-wireless/wpa_supplicant dbus
media-libs/freetype harfbuzz
media-libs/libglvnd X
# sway needs a seat: logind (elogind) is the session manager on this profile, so the PAM stack must register login
# sessions with it (pambase) and libseat needs its logind backend (seatd). Without these sway fails with
# "Failed to start a DRM session" (found by the QEMU test: the stock binpkgs have both flags off).
sys-auth/pambase elogind
sys-auth/seatd elogind
